            "review_title": "Review at Vinh Steak 'n Ale",
            "review_text": "VuThiAn\nBrecksville, OH5 contributions\n0\nBest Steak in Vietnam\nJul 2019\nWe are Vietnamese Americans who return to visit Vietnam about once a year. Saigon (as we expats prefer to call it instead of HCM city) has zillions of restaurants to choose from. But most western style restaurants are usually located in western style hotels. They are pricey and the foods are barely palatable. For those who are well traveled and price conscious, Vinh Steak 'n Ale offers a great alternative. They even pleased our friend who is an expat from France. A combination of imported special cuts of steak from the US and Australia with many selections of Ale flavors, helps make Vinh Steak 'n Ale stand out among numerous eateries in this very populated city.\n\nSince we were a large group, we ordered all kinds of steaks, prepared from rare to well-done and all the different savory sauces. They did not disappoint. Personally, I love their Italian style garlic bread.\n\nThe special treat for me was their freshly made \"nước cóc,\" or ambarella juice. My friend's families all ordered second or third glass of this delicious, refreshing juice. \n\nFor those who prefer to stay in, or tired of eating ordinary lunch but has no time to go out, I heard they also offer delivery through Grab.\n\nVinh Steak 'n Ale offers many other dishes. We just have to return to try them all on our next trip to Vietnam.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 22, 2019\nVinh Steak 'n Ale\nDear Ms. VuThiAn,\n\nSincerest thanks for dining with us, and it was our great pleasure to serving you.\n\nWe are very delighted to know that you have had a great dining experience in our restaurant. Such comment like yours makes us feel so rewarded for all the endeavors we put into the job.\n\nWe are looking forward to welcoming you again in near future.\n\nBest regards,\n\nVinh Steak ‘n Ale Team\nRead more\nWritten September 25, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
