            "review_title": "Review at Vinh Steak 'n Ale",
            "review_text": "FellowTraveler81314\n1 contribution\n1\nBest \"Western-styled\" Steak at Affordable Price in Town.\nJul 2019\nBest steaks in Saigon. Tender, juicy and so tasty. No wonder: The steaks are imported from the US and Australia.\n\nThree steak sauce can accompany the steak: Pepper, mushroom and mustard. The sauce are made from scratch and Chef Vinh's special recipe. We tried all the sauce and particularly like the pepper sauce. It was simply delicious and paired well with the steak. \n\nFor dessert we tried the creme brulee, another Chef Vinh's secret recipe. It was simply delicious.\n\nFor beverage we tried all the ale on the menu. Ale, one of Charles Dickens' favorite drink, unlike beer, is something that generally unheard of in Vietnam and rarely found in restaurants in Vietnam. From the ale list, we particularly liked Pacific Pilsner and Belle Passion Fruit.\n\nThe restaurant is simple decorated and cozy, more intimate than most restaurants. \n\nThe staff is friendly, courteous and extremely helpful. It showed the eagerness to serve and please. Some even speak English.\n\nThe biggest surprise came at the end of our dinner at Vinh Steak 'n Ale when Phuong, the hostess presented us the check: It was very reasonable considering the high quality \"Western style\" food and drink and, quite appropriate with the restaurant's slogan \"US beef - Vietnamese price\"\n\nOn a scale of tale we rated Vinh Steak 'n Ale 9.5. We will come back with more friends to try other extraordinary dishes on the menu on our next trip to Vietnam.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 22, 2019\nVinh Steak 'n Ale\nDear Mrs. / Mr. FellowTraveler81314,\n\nSincerest thanks for dining with us, and it was our great pleasure to serving you.\n\nWe are very delighted to know that you have had a great dining experience in our restaurant. Such comment like yours makes us feel so rewarded for all the endeavors we put into the job.\n\nWe are looking forward to welcoming you again in near future.\n\nBest regards,\n\nVinh Steak ‘n Ale Team\nRead more\nWritten September 25, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
